    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="1001" n="983" sameAs="frus:frus1947v03/pg983"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">865.24/9–1147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Embassy in Italy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-27T11:00:00-04:00">September 27,
                            1947—11 a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1863. Army Survey Group (ASGI) under Col Bathurst<anchor n="1" xml:id="d650-f1"/>
                    proceeding Italy Sept 27 to undertake thorough review reequipment program Ital
                    Army and also to study all aspects possible desirability and practicability
                    establishment US Military Mission Ital Govt. Decision send Group largely result
                    consideration, in consultation with Dept, points urtel 2718 Sept 11. Mission has
                    full support Gen Lee who discussed matter with Group yesterday. Col Bathurst
                    will advise you his instructions and will undertake survey in closest
                    consultation you and Emb staff. Army informing MA who will give you further
                    details ASGI mission.</p>
                <p>Re establishment US Mil Mission Italy, Dept has formulated no firm position but
                    will appreciate your views desirability from political point of view after you
                    have considered recommendations ASGI report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d650-f1" n="1" xml:id="d650-f1-content">
                <p>Col. Charles R. Bathurst, executive officer, Organization and Training Division,
                    General Staff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
